counterfactuals.output:
A deformation measurement method comprising:

providing a sheet including a first layer portion and a second layer portion, the first layer portion having a plurality of first lines arranged in parallel with each other, and the second layer portion having a plurality of second lines extending in a direction different from a direction in which the first lines extend;

attaching the sheet to a measurement target;

acquiring an image of the sheet before and/or after deformation of the measurement target;

detecting, from the acquired image, a positional change or a shape change of at least one of the first lines and the second lines; and

calculating a deformation amount or a deformation direction of the measurement target based on the detected positional change or shape change,

wherein the deformation of the measurement target is measured by using a change in an apparent pattern formed by superposition or crossing of the first lines and the second lines.
